  <!-- Why -->
  <section id="why" class="section" aria-labelledby="why-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-end">
        <h2 id="why-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">Molecular diagnostics without the limits of conventional testing</h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">Conventional genetic tests need venous blood, a cold chain, a specialist laboratory and a second test to confirm. So they rarely reach the people who need them most.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="why mt-12">
        <li><h3>A spot of blood, not a tube</h3><p>A finger prick onto a card. No venepuncture, no EDTA tube, no pre-processing.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Room temperature, not a cold chain</h3><p>Cards keep and travel at room temperature, so samples can come from anywhere a health worker can reach.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Screening and confirmation in one</h3><p>One test does both, so a positive result needs no second test and no second visit.*</p></li>
        <li><h3>Extraction-free molecular diagnostics</h3><p>No separate DNA extraction step, which saves a laboratory time and reagents.*</p></li>
        <li><h3>From birth</h3><p>Newborns can be tested at birth. Conventional confirmatory tests wait 72 hours.*</p></li>
        <li><h3>Minimal laboratory infrastructure</h3><p>Standard PCR equipment and a gel tank. No specialised laboratory.</p></li>
        <li><h3>High-throughput, automation-friendly</h3><p>Many cards in one run, on a workflow that can be automated.</p></li>
        <li><h3>For one patient or a whole district</h3><p>Designed for a diagnosis in a clinic and for large-scale public health programmes.</p></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="footnote">* Where applicable for developed assays.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

